Z||000011||TheDobe88GT||08-26-2001||12:14 AM||||Hey, how's about posting the address/phone number or web site for the various sources of those new crate engines.  I'm looking for a 3.4 for my 87 and would love to get one for that price range!||||reg||1
Z||000012||cultcar||08-26-2001||10:42 AM||||There are a few nationwide suppliers of remanufactured motors.  Your supplier's cost is due to the 3 year warranty.  Recon (check website) distributes through Advanced Auto and offers their 2.8 for $900 with only a 1 year warranty.  I had a Fiero-loving certified mechanic install mine and it has been smooth for almost a year now.  Before you buy any motor, it MUST come with a Cam card, or timing card.  If it doesn't, don't buy it.  It's your only guarantee that it has the correct cam for the High Output version of the 2.8 that came in Fieros.  Otherwise, you will have to get your mechanic to measure the cam movement to validate.  And if it's wrong, you will have to return the motor.  Voice of experience here.  $2200 overall is good.  Mine reached $2500 because of unforeseen things.  Be ready to pay for them now.  Don't skimp and regret it later.<P>Ron||||reg||1
